{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792777802,"nonce":"HtIIk6MlSXWwL2YQEFpBsNMa14k=","title":"zynml: hot reload no longer migrates a running loop on a Cranelift-only ladder","message":"`hot_reload_loop_boundary::a_running_loop_finishes_in_the_edited_code` (\"no iteration ran the edited step; the loop never migrated\") and `hot_reload_fibers::a_suspended_fiber_keeps_its_state_and_picks_up_the_edit` fail on main (NUC, release). 7006a9f5 made `loop_probes` emit back-edge probes only when LLVM is the top tier, but a running loop also moves into a reloaded body through those probes, and these runtimes enable hot reload on the default Cranelift ladder.\n\n`hot_reload_effect_fibers::a_running_machine_observes_the_edited_event_source` fails separately on timing: its machine's million transitions finish inside the test's 100 ms wait on a release build, so the reload lands after the run (\"every event carried the old value\", count = 1000000). With a machine ten times longer it passes in 0.2 s.","files":null}]}